A poor couple each secretly sell their dearest treasure to buy a gift for the other, only to find the gifts unusable yet proof of the deepest love.

1. Poor Love Rich Pride  (passages 1-2)
    A broke young wife desperate to honor her husband discovers their only riches are her long
    hair and his heirloom watch.
       -> Loving him so much with so little money drives her to give up her own treasure.
2. Selling Hair for Chain  (passages 3-3)
    She sells her hair to buy him a fine platinum chain for his watch and fixes what remains.
       -> Coming home transformed forces an anxious wait for how Jim will see her.
3. Tense Reunion Turns Tender  (passages 4-5)
    She fears he no longer finds her pretty, but he insists his love is unchanged and gives her
    his own wrapped present.
       -> His mysterious package promises joy but hides a matching sacrifice that must be
       revealed.
4. Mutual Sacrifice Proved Wisest  (passages 6-6)
    His present turns out to be combs for her gone hair, bought by selling his watch, so their
    useless gifts become the wisest love.
